(1558299, 204817, 30364, '<td valign="top">Originally posted by lots of folks:<br/>"Too purple, too pink, blah, blah, blah ..."<br/> <br/>Bullshit.  Why should every photograph exhibit colour fidelity?  This is dusk.  Dusk is evening.  Evening is velvet.  Velvet is this colour.  I don''t want to go over the top here, especially as Robert says it''s a bit of a throw-away shot for him, but PLEASE have a look at a couple of Van Gough paintings ... do you imagine Vincent''s colours and textures are high-fidelity?</td>', 'Originally posted by lots of folks:"Too purple, too pink, blah, blah, blah ..." Bullshit.  Why should every photograph exhibit colour fidelity?  This is dusk.  Dusk is evening.  Evening is velvet.  Velvet is this colour.  I don''t want to go over the top here, especially as Robert says it''s a bit of a throw-away shot for him, but PLEASE have a look at a couple of Van Gough paintings ... do you imagine Vincent''s colours and textures are high-fidelity?', '2005-07-24 02:17:34.000000', NULL, 0),
