(1558627, 202730, 25553, '<td valign="top">darn.. didnt vote on this one but wouldve surely scored you high for not shooting a flag or a bald eagle. love the lighting and how they make her contours flow. keep up the good work. <br/> <br/>ps-have you ever read Ayn Rand''s definition of photography? its quite interesting.</td>', 'darn.. didnt vote on this one but wouldve surely scored you high for not shooting a flag or a bald eagle. love the lighting and how they make her contours flow. keep up the good work.  ps-have you ever read Ayn Rand''s definition of photography? its quite interesting.', '2005-07-24 11:15:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558633, 203731, 15711, '<td valign="top">Top 20 !! Way to go.  I thought this was one of those millisecond captures that worked perfectly.  Science and art combined - gee whiz, what could be better than that/?? :~)</td>', 'Top 20 !! Way to go.  I thought this was one of those millisecond captures that worked perfectly.  Science and art combined - gee whiz, what could be better than that/?? :~)', '2005-07-24 11:24:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558635, 204028, 15711, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote this high, but heh, it was extremely original and I give you kudos for that.  People get so up in arms over the dumbest things.  Nobody has your number memorized, so if they went to the trouble to look it up to find out who you are, then they are more of a sleuth than I.<br/> <br/>Kee up the unique aspect to your work!!!</td>', 'I didn''t vote this high, but heh, it was extremely original and I give you kudos for that.  People get so up in arms over the dumbest things.  Nobody has your number memorized, so if they went to the trouble to look it up to find out who you are, then they are more of a sleuth than I. Kee up the unique aspect to your work!!!', '2005-07-24 11:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558642, 202575, 15711, '<td valign="top">I love reading the descriptions after a challenge.  This is a great shot, and I find it even better, knowing the situation under which you took it.  YOU GO GIRL!! Nice lighting and perspective. I''m intrigued by the fact that it''s almost that yin and yang with shadow to the left and light to the right. Very cool. The overall composition is simple and uncluttered. Much like how a snake lives his life. (Oh wow, I''m getting way too deep here). <br/> <br/>You''ve got more nerve than me.  Reptiles??? NO thanks - give me something with fur any day.</td>', 'I love reading the descriptions after a challenge.  This is a great shot, and I find it even better, knowing the situation under which you took it.  YOU GO GIRL!! Nice lighting and perspective. I''m intrigued by the fact that it''s almost that yin and yang with shadow to the left and light to the right. Very cool. The overall composition is simple and uncluttered. Much like how a snake lives his life. (Oh wow, I''m getting way too deep here).  You''ve got more nerve than me.  Reptiles??? NO thanks - give me something with fur any day.', '2005-07-24 11:31:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558644, 204798, 15711, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Rob.  I reiterate what I said in my original post. This is interesting and effective all the way around.  Great finish for you!!!</td>', 'Congratulations Rob.  I reiterate what I said in my original post. This is interesting and effective all the way around.  Great finish for you!!!', '2005-07-24 11:32:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558668, 204479, 36231, '<td valign="top">Visit this tutorial to help you with how to prepare a photo.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">How to prepare a photo for DPC</a> <br/> <br/>This had really helped me out a lot. :)</td>', 'Visit this tutorial to help you with how to prepare a photo. How to prepare a photo for DPC  This had really helped me out a lot. :)', '2005-07-24 12:01:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558682, 204845, 5112, '<td valign="top">Hi, thank you!<br/> <br/>@skiprow - simple panning:  I set the camera to Shutter Priority, set the shutter speed to 1/30 sec, manually focused on the girl/swing.  Then I got the girl swinging, started following the movement with my camera trying to keep her hed in my view all the time.  Then depress the shutter while panning (moving the camera at the same speed as the swing).<br/> <br/>Very little post-processing:  cropped a bit, worked on histogram/curves to get the colours a bit more vibrant, resized, sharpened, applied a light noise remover (very light) overall to smoothen the whole thing.<br/> <br/>Hope that helps!</td>', 'Hi, thank you! @skiprow - simple panning:  I set the camera to Shutter Priority, set the shutter speed to 1/30 sec, manually focused on the girl/swing.  Then I got the girl swinging, started following the movement with my camera trying to keep her hed in my view all the time.  Then depress the shutter while panning (moving the camera at the same speed as the swing). Very little post-processing:  cropped a bit, worked on histogram/curves to get the colours a bit more vibrant, resized, sharpened, applied a light noise remover (very light) overall to smoothen the whole thing. Hope that helps!', '2005-07-24 12:22:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558695, 203731, 36616, '<td valign="top">I stillthink this is the best shot in the comp. Well done</td>', 'I stillthink this is the best shot in the comp. Well done', '2005-07-24 12:30:08.000000', NULL, 0),
