(1559957, 202394, 9581, '<td valign="top">Looks brand new straight from the package.... I love it, its got its own thing going on that it doesnt need anything else with it for a subject. Heres just a thought and a few tips of suggestions for future shooting..One thing is for sure I am not perfect, I try but it takes someone to point a few things out...<br/> <br/> For all that voted low on this perhaps maybe they didnt like the creases from when it was folded there in  the flag. A iron, or putting this in the dryer with a damp cloth for 5 minutes might of helped the lines to flatten out... Looks as though when you folded  the flag over or spiraled it a bit that the flag sord of made a small shadow cast not much..  Where was your light coming from, you may have been able to add another lamp to help this out or use a strong flashlight in front of it.. I sometimes have atleast 2 flash lights, and now I have narrowed it down to 3 lamps that are portable for my area that I do all my portraits and subject shooting.. You dont always need them but its fun to play and experiment with them.. <br/>I hope I havent picked to much, its a very cool image.. congratulations on making it to 6.0... :) I hope I do this next challenge for wood.. <br/></td>', 'Looks brand new straight from the package.... I love it, its got its own thing going on that it doesnt need anything else with it for a subject. Heres just a thought and a few tips of suggestions for future shooting..One thing is for sure I am not perfect, I try but it takes someone to point a few things out...  For all that voted low on this perhaps maybe they didnt like the creases from when it was folded there in  the flag. A iron, or putting this in the dryer with a damp cloth for 5 minutes might of helped the lines to flatten out... Looks as though when you folded  the flag over or spiraled it a bit that the flag sord of made a small shadow cast not much..  Where was your light coming from, you may have been able to add another lamp to help this out or use a strong flashlight in front of it.. I sometimes have atleast 2 flash lights, and now I have narrowed it down to 3 lamps that are portable for my area that I do all my portraits and subject shooting.. You dont always need them but its fun to play and experiment with them.. I hope I havent picked to much, its a very cool image.. congratulations on making it to 6.0... :) I hope I do this next challenge for wood.. ', '2005-07-25 00:51:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1560056, 204676, 8981, '<td valign="top">Wow Aimz!  You''re pictures just keep getting better and better!  This is a great shot!  Congrats on your top 40 placing!  Keep up the great work!</td>', 'Wow Aimz!  You''re pictures just keep getting better and better!  This is a great shot!  Congrats on your top 40 placing!  Keep up the great work!', '2005-07-25 01:03:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1560462, 203969, 37673, '<td valign="top">This is a little difficult to critique.  There are too many ways in which you can view this photo. The colors are very dramatic as is the statement. It conveys an array of emotions depending on the viewers state of mind. It could be anger or happiness, victory or defeat. It could mean acceptance or defiance. My immediate impression was victory due to my state of mind. As I viewed it later other emotions and impressions came to mind. I like it beacause of the diverse meanings. On a technical note  it may have been over saturated and a bit too much contrast. Composition is great. Lighting was very creative. I would like to see the original to compare what has been done. The focus could have been better but I think all of these issues can be cast aside if you are viewing from another perspective. It meets and falls short of so many different planes. Over all I really enjoy the picture and would love to see more like it.  Very fine job.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'This is a little difficult to critique.  There are too many ways in which you can view this photo. The colors are very dramatic as is the statement. It conveys an array of emotions depending on the viewers state of mind. It could be anger or happiness, victory or defeat. It could mean acceptance or defiance. My immediate impression was victory due to my state of mind. As I viewed it later other emotions and impressions came to mind. I like it beacause of the diverse meanings. On a technical note  it may have been over saturated and a bit too much contrast. Composition is great. Lighting was very creative. I would like to see the original to compare what has been done. The focus could have been better but I think all of these issues can be cast aside if you are viewing from another perspective. It meets and falls short of so many different planes. Over all I really enjoy the picture and would love to see more like it.  Very fine job.  Keep up the good work.', '2005-07-25 02:12:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1560466, 203167, 28108, '<td valign="top">This is really cool. The light is great. Love the title</td>', 'This is really cool. The light is great. Love the title', '2005-07-25 02:13:44.000000', NULL, 0),
