(1561954, 204559, 32792, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Titia:</b></div><hr/><i> It''s a beautiful photo and it might say ''Independence'' to all Americans, but being a Dutchie an eagle head is not a symbol of anything, it''s nothing else than just an ''eagle head'' and therefor to me: it didn''t meet the challenge. That''s one of the reasons I decided not to vote at all on this challenge.<br/> <br/>Nevertheless, congrats with the blue ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I do share the same opinion! It''s an outstanding image. But it doesn''t scream independence to me. This might work for the north-american (I''m also american) fellows, but not quite that much for the rest of the world! I know it''s the american symbol for it, but what about the rest of us "non-north american" ppl?<br/>Still a great show, and a great example of what the Sigma 105mm can do! That lens is deffinatelly on my list....</td>', 'Originally posted by Titia: It''s a beautiful photo and it might say ''Independence'' to all Americans, but being a Dutchie an eagle head is not a symbol of anything, it''s nothing else than just an ''eagle head'' and therefor to me: it didn''t meet the challenge. That''s one of the reasons I decided not to vote at all on this challenge. Nevertheless, congrats with the blue ribbon.  I do share the same opinion! It''s an outstanding image. But it doesn''t scream independence to me. This might work for the north-american (I''m also american) fellows, but not quite that much for the rest of the world! I know it''s the american symbol for it, but what about the rest of us "non-north american" ppl?Still a great show, and a great example of what the Sigma 105mm can do! That lens is deffinatelly on my list....', '2005-07-25 15:29:23.000000', NULL, 0),
